{"name":"Natural Evolution","hex":"#a27833","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"natural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing in nature.","Normally associated with a particular person or thing; inherently related to the nature of a thing or creature."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native inhabitant of a place, country, etc.","A note that is not or is no longer to be modified by an accidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural"},{"term":"evolution","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A change of position.","An unfolding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolution"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evolution","blocks":[{"text":"Evolution is the change in the heritable characteristics of biological populations over successive generations. It happens when individuals in a population vary in their genetic characteristics and in the numbers of their surviving offspring. Mutation introduces new genetic variation, and processes such as genetic drift, gene flow, and natural selection result in some genetic variants becoming more or less common over time. Evolution is often defined as a change in the frequency of alleles in a population."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Darwin_Tree_1837.png/330px-Darwin_Tree_1837.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evolution","wikidata":"Q1063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Darwin_Tree_1837.png/500px-Darwin_Tree_1837.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Darwin_Tree_1837.png/1280px-Darwin_Tree_1837.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Darwin_Tree_1837.png/500px-Darwin_Tree_1837.png?utm_source=en.wi